      "content": "In addition to influencing flavor, yeast can also produce stress signals that can trigger bacteria to produce more acidity, or vice versa. Poor temperature, contamination, insufficient feeding, or over-mixing the starter can stress or kill yeast cells, creating an environment that favors bacterial growth and reduces yeast activity. If yeast is killed or severely stressed, the starter can become over-acidified, creating an environment that hampered yeast growth and leading to starter decline or even death.",
